§ `Section 672.45 -- Hearing to be held by a court`

-- 672.45(1): where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered in respect of an accused, the court may of its own motion, and shall on application by the accused or the prosecutor, hold a disposition hearing.
-- Two limbs: the permission (of its own motion) and the duty (on application). Both are gated by the "where a verdict ... is rendered".
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13534 | 672.45 (1) Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered in respect of an accused, the court may of its own motion, and shall on application by the accused or the prosecutor, hold a disposition hearing.
@ref s 672.45(1) (src:13534)
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.45(1) the court may of its own motion hold a disposition hearing` MEANS
    IF `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered in respect of the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered in respect of an accused"

