    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied that it can readily do so and that a disposition should be made without delay"

§ `Section 672.46 -- Status quo pending Review Board hearing`

-- 672.46(1): if the court does not make a disposition in respect of the accused at a disposition hearing, any order for the detention of the accused or any release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking in respect of the accused that is in force at the time the verdict is rendered
-- continues in force, subject to its terms, until the Review Board makes a disposition.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13540 | 672.46 (1) If the court does not make a disposition in respect of the accused at a disposition hearing, any order for the detention of the accused or any release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking in respect of the accused that is in force at the time the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered continues in force, subject to its terms, until the Review Board makes a disposition.
@ref s 672.46(1) (src:13540)
GIVEN `the court does not make a disposition at a disposition hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking is in force at the time the verdict is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board has made a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.46(1) the order, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking continues in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the court does not make a disposition at a disposition hearing` AND `the order, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking is in force at the time the verdict is rendered`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court does not make a disposition in respect of the accused at a disposition hearing"
        IF `the Review Board has made a disposition` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the Review Board makes a disposition"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 672.46(2): despite (1), a court may, pending a disposition by the Review Board, on cause being shown, vacate the detention order, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking, and make any other order for the detention of the accused or any other release order
-- that it considers appropriate, including an order that the accused be detained in custody in a hospital.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13542 | (2) Despite subsection (1), a court may, pending a disposition by the Review Board in respect of the accused, on cause being shown, vacate the detention order, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking referred to in that subsection, and make any other order for the detention of the accused or any other release order that the court considers to be appropriate in the circumstances, including an order directing that the accused be detained in custody in a hospital.
@ref s 672.46(2) (src:13542)
GIVEN `the Review Board has not yet made a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cause is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.46(2) the court may vacate the order and make another order for detention or release` MEANS
    IF `the Review Board has not yet made a disposition` AND `cause is shown`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a court may, pending a disposition by the Review Board in respect of the accused, on cause being shown, vacate the detention order"

§ `Section 672.47 -- Review Board to make disposition where court does not`

-- 672.47(1): where a verdict of NCR or unfit is rendered and the court makes no disposition, the Review Board shall, as soon as is practicable but not later than forty-five days after the verdict was rendered, hold a hearing and make a disposition.
-- As a regulative rule: the Review Board's duty, within 45 days of the verdict. "As soon as practicable" has no number and is not modelled in the rule.
-- src:13544 | 672.47 (1) Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered and the court makes no disposition in respect of an accused, the Review Board shall, as soon as is practicable but not later than forty-five days after the verdict was rendered, hold a hearing and make a disposition.
@ref s 672.47(1) (src:13544)
DECLARE `s 672.47 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.47 hold a hearing and make a disposition`

@ref s 672.47(1) (src:13544)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 672.47 act`
`s 672.47(1) the Review Board must hold a hearing within forty-five days after the verdict` MEANS
    PARTY `a Review Board`
    MUST `s 672.47 hold a hearing and make a disposition`
    WITHIN 45
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a Review Board` BECAUSE "no hearing was held and no disposition made within forty-five days after the verdict"

-- 672.47(2): where the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it, the court may extend the time for holding a hearing under (1) to a maximum of ninety days after the verdict was rendered.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE, F-CAP
-- src:13546 | (2) Where the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it, the court may extend the time for holding a hearing under subsection (1) to a maximum of ninety days after the verdict was rendered.
@ref s 672.47(2) (src:13546)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days after the verdict to which the time is extended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.47(2) the court may extend the time for holding the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it` AND `the days after the verdict to which the time is extended` AT MOST 90
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it, the court may extend the time for holding a hearing under subsection (1) to a maximum of ninety days after the verdict was rendered"

-- The duty of (1) as a decision function over dates, with the extension of (2): the hearing must be held not later than 45 days after the verdict, or 90 if the court has extended the time.
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13544 | 672.47 (1) Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered and the court makes no disposition in respect of an accused, the Review Board shall, as soon as is practicable but not later than forty-five days after the verdict was rendered, hold a hearing and make a disposition.
-- src:13545 | Extension of time for hearing
-- src:13546 | (2) Where the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it, the court may extend the time for holding a hearing under subsection (1) to a maximum of ninety days after the verdict was rendered.
@ref s 672.47(1); s 672.47(2) (src:13544-13546)
