§ `Sections 672.48 and 672.49 -- Review Board and fitness; continued detention`

-- 672.48(1): where a Review Board holds a hearing to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused who has been found unfit to stand trial, it shall determine whether in its opinion the accused is fit to stand trial at the time of the hearing.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13554 | 672.48 (1) Where a Review Board holds a hearing to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused who has been found unfit to stand trial, it shall determine whether in its opinion the accused is fit to stand trial at the time of the hearing.
@ref s 672.48(1) (src:13554)
GIVEN `a Review Board holds a hearing to make or review a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been found unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.48(1) the Review Board must determine whether the accused is fit to stand trial at the time of the hearing` MEANS
    IF `a Review Board holds a hearing to make or review a disposition` AND `the accused has been found unfit to stand trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a Review Board holds a hearing to make or review a disposition in respect of an accused who has been found unfit to stand trial"

-- 672.48(2): if a Review Board determines that the accused is fit to stand trial, it shall order that the accused be sent back to court, and the court shall try the issue and render a verdict.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13556 | (2) If a Review Board determines that the accused is fit to stand trial, it shall order that the accused be sent back to court, and the court shall try the issue and render a verdict.
@ref s 672.48(2) (src:13556)
GIVEN `the Review Board determines that the accused is fit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.48(2) the Review Board must order that the accused be sent back to court` MEANS
    IF `the Review Board determines that the accused is fit to stand trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a Review Board determines that the accused is fit to stand trial"

-- 672.48(3): the chairperson of a Review Board may, with the consent of the accused and the person in charge of the hospital where the accused is being detained, order that the accused be sent back to court for trial of the issue of whether the accused is unfit to stand trial,
-- where the chairperson is of the opinion that (a) the accused is fit to stand trial; and (b) the Review Board will not hold a hearing to make or review a disposition within a reasonable period.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13558 | (3) The chairperson of a Review Board may, with the consent of the accused and the person in charge of the hospital where an accused is being detained, order that the accused be sent back to court for trial of the issue of whether the accused is unfit to stand trial, where the chairperson is of the opinion that
-- src:13559 | (a) the accused is fit to stand trial; and
-- src:13560 | (b) the Review Board will not hold a hearing to make or review a disposition in respect of the accused within a reasonable period.
